build/
.build/

# Compiler intermediates. Running swiftc by hand in the repo root drops four of these per source
# file beside Package.swift; a hundred of them were committed that way once. Build through
# `swift build` or `build.sh`, which keep everything under .build/.
*.o
*.d
*.dia
*.swiftdeps
*.swiftmodule
*.swiftdoc
*.swiftsourceinfo
*.dmg
.DS_Store

# Credentials. Nothing in this repo ever needs an App Store Connect private key on disk — the key
# lives in the Keychain — but a stray AuthKey_XXXXXXXX.p8 in the working directory is the single
# worst thing that could be committed here, so it is excluded defensively and by shape.
*.p8
AuthKey_*

# Real reports and the on-disk cache, in case anyone points the app's Application Support path here
# or unzips a downloaded report to poke at it. Fixtures under Tests/Fixtures/ are synthetic and are
# committed deliberately; these are not.
*.gz
S_D_*.txt
Application Support/

# Local working materials, not part of the published repo
VANTAGE_PLAN.md

# Implementation plans are scaffolding: step-by-step instructions for work that has since happened,
# written against a codebase that has since moved. They are useful on a branch and a liability on
# main, where they age into confident wrong statements in a directory that looks like documentation.
# The design specs beside them are kept and committed — those record why, which the code can't.
docs/superpowers/plans/
